      "content": "Relief from a headache medication strongly suggests a migraine, but it does not completely rule out all serious possibilities. Some less common, severe conditions can mimic migraine pain and might temporarily lessen with pain medication. Because the sudden, severe onset is concerning, the safest course of action is to consult a medical professional, even if it's not the ER right now. A quick telehealth call can offer professional guidance on whether waiting is safe or if an in-person visit is necessary.",
